  "notes": "{良|よ}い is an i-adjective meaning \"good\" with an irregular form いい used in everyday speech.\n\nFORMS:\n- Dictionary: よい or いい (いい is more casual)\n- Negative: よくない (NOT いくない)\n- Past: よかった (NOT いかった)\n- Adverb: よく (well, often)\n\nGRAMMAR PATTERNS:\n- 〜てもいい/よい: may ~, it's okay to ~\n- 〜ばよかった: should have ~ (regret)\n- 〜なくてもいい: don't have to ~\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {天気|てんき}がいい: good weather\n- {頭|あたま}がいい: smart\n- {体|からだ}にいい: good for the body\n- {仲|なか}がいい: on good terms\n- {運|うん}がいい: lucky\n\nIMPORTANT:\nAlways conjugate from よ-, not い-. \"It was good\" = よかった, not いかった.",
